Fix $n\ge2$ and $0<\delta<1/10$, and put $L_*=1.004$. There are constants $W,T\ge1$, depending only on $n,\delta$, with the following property. Let $h_0$ be a complete smooth metric on a manifold $M^n$ without boundary, let $h\ge h_0$ be smooth, and let $t\ge T$ be smooth. Let $A$ be a nonempty compact set and $B$ a nonempty closed set such that $$\mathop{\mathrm{dist}}_{h_0}(A,B)\ge W.$$ For every $0<d<\delta$ there are smooth $h'\ge h$ and $t'\ge t$ such that the changes have compact support in $\{\mathop{\mathrm{dist}}_{h_0}(A,\cdot)<W\}$, $$\label{step:conclusion}
 \mathcal D(h',t')\ge \mathcal D(h,t)+(t'^2-t^2)
 -\delta\bigl(\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}_h h_0-\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}_{h'}h_0\bigr)t'^2-dt'^2,$$ and $$\label{step:distance}
 \mathop{\mathrm{dist}}_{h'}(A,B)\ge L_*W.$$ In particular, $h'$ is complete. Neither $W$ nor $T$ depends on $d$, the geometry of $M$, or the sets $A,B$.

On this original neighborhood, the raw output satisfies $$\label{step:raw-inequality}
 \mathcal D(h_u,t_u)\ge\mathcal D(h,t)+(t_u^2-t^2)
 -\delta(\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}_hh_0-\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}_{h_u}h_0)t_u^2-\frac d2t^2.$$

Suppose that $h_0$ is a complete metric, $t_0\ge T$ is smooth, and $$\mathcal D(h_0,t_0)\ge c+t_0^2$$ for a constant $c$. Let $(A_i,B_i)$ be a finite or countable family of nonempty closed pairs, with each $A_i$ compact and $\mathop{\mathrm{dist}}_{h_0}(A_i,B_i)\ge W$. Suppose there are locally finite compact sets $K_i$ such that the open $h_0$-distance-$W$ neighborhood of $A_i$ is contained in $K_i\setminus B_i$. Then there are smooth $h_1\ge h_0$ and $t_1\ge t_0$, obtained by a locally finite sequence of compactly supported changes inside the $K_i$, such that $$\begin{aligned}
 \mathop{\mathrm{dist}}_{h_1}(A_i,B_i)&\ge L_*W \quad\text{for every }i,\label{rounds:separation}\\
 \mathcal D(h_1,t_1)&\ge c+
 \bigl(1-(n+1)\delta\bigr)t_1^2.\label{rounds:curvature}
\end{aligned}$$ The metric $h_1$ is complete.

If $B$ is a $d$-fold further face of $E$, the product projection sends $D_E$ in that tail into $D_B$. At a split of label $j_0$ on a parent of dimension $m$, suppose the remaining cores have been enlarged, giving $G'_j\subset G_j$ for $j\ne j_0$, and define the closed guard $$\label{packet:guard}
 H_E^*=\bigl\{x:\#\{j\in J_r\setminus\{j_0\}:x\in G'_j\}
                      \ge m-2\bigr\}.$$ Suppose a regular zero wall $L$ lies in $\operatorname{int}G_{j_0}$. Pull the remaining cores to a new side or hit packet $A$ by bulk inclusion, wall restriction, and projection of the attached cylinder. Define $D_A$ using these cores, the remaining labels, and the dimension of $A$, as in <a href="#packet:required-set" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="packet:required-set">[packet:required-set]</a>. Then $D_A$ projects into both $H_E^*$ and the parent’s old set $D_E$. Guards likewise project into guards on further faces.

Equip a packet diagram after the radial stage with compatible smooth base metrics and finitely many compatible smooth positive warp functions. Each connected packet $E$, separately, is complete and has bounded geometry: positive injectivity radius and bounds on curvature and every covariant derivative. Every warp and all its covariant derivatives are bounded on $E$, and every warp has a positive lower bound. For $\omega_E$ the product of the warps there are constants $A_E<\infty$ and an integer $d_E\le\dim E$ such that $$\label{packet:growth}
 \int_{B_E(x,R)}\omega_E\,\mathrm d\mathop{\mathrm{vol}}_E
       \le A_E(1+R)^{d_E}
       \qquad(x\in E,\ R\ge0).$$ The constant is uniform over centers in this packet. The same assertions hold on $E\times\mathbb R^a$, with the product metric, pulled-back warps, and growth exponent at most $d_E+a$, for every finite $a$.

There is a smooth finite compatible function $p_0$ and a number $c_*>0$ such that every $p=p_0+c$, $|c|<c_*$, satisfies $$\label{cut:pressure-gradient}
             2|\mathop{\mathrm{grad}}p|\le .67p^2+1.02\Pi_{j_0}.$$ There are compatible smooth barrier domains $D^+,D^-$ whose interiors contain the corresponding forced-core closures and whose closures lie in the respective pole interiors. Each admits a smooth vector field $Y^\pm$ with $|Y^\pm|\le1$, equal to the outward unit normal on its boundary, such that, for all these shifts, $$\label{cut:barrier-pressure}
 p\ge1+\mathop{\mathrm{div}}_\omega Y^+\quad\hbox{on }D^+,
 \qquad
 -p\ge1+\mathop{\mathrm{div}}_\omega Y^-\quad\hbox{on }D^-.$$ After the radial split all this data has bounded derivatives on each packet. At the initial radial split the barriers are the separate relatively compact domains in the radial pole bands, and the choices are locally finite with locally prescribed bounds.

Let $A$ satisfy <a href="#cut:local-minimality" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="cut:local-minimality">[cut:local-minimality]</a> on a smooth $m$-manifold, $m\ge2$, with smooth positive $\omega$ and smooth $p$. Put $S=\mathop{\mathrm{supp}}|D\chi_A|$. Then $S=S_{\rm reg}\cup\Sigma$, where $S_{\rm reg}$ is a smooth embedded hypersurface, $\Sigma$ is relatively closed, and $$\label{cut:singular-dimension}
                         \dim_{\mathcal H}\Sigma\le m-8.$$ A negative dimension bound means that $\Sigma$ is empty. The outward measure-theoretic normal extends smoothly on $S_{\rm reg}$. With $B(u,v)=\langle\nabla_u\nu,v\rangle$, its base mean curvature satisfies $$\label{cut:base-mean-curvature}
                    H_g=p-\partial_\nu\log\omega.$$ The unweighted multiplicity-one perimeter varifold has locally bounded generalized mean curvature. Its density exists at every support point; monotonicity gives local uniform area upper bounds and positive area lower bounds at support points. Under the convergences of <a href="#cut:bv-compactness" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="cut:bv-compactness">39</a>, densities are upper semicontinuous at converging points, provided the local generalized-mean-curvature bounds are uniform. The supports converge locally, and on every compact subset of the regular limiting hypersurface convergence is smooth and single-sheeted when the data converge smoothly. On compact subsets of the interiors of the limiting phases there is eventually no boundary.*

*Every tangent at a point of $S$ is a multiplicity-one locally perimeter-minimizing boundary cone in the Euclidean tangent space. A flat tangent implies regularity. A tangent at a singular point is therefore nonflat, and its translation-invariance spine has dimension at most $m-8$.

For every compactly supported smooth invariant test $v$ on $S$, $$\label{cut:wall-form}
 \int_S\bigl(2|\mathop{\mathrm{grad}}v|^2+R_Sv^2\bigr)\,\mathrm d\mu_S
 \ge\int_S\bigl(R+p^2+|B|^2+2\partial_\nu p\bigr)v^2\,\mathrm d\mu_S.$$ In particular its right side is at least $\int_S(R-1.02\Pi_{j_0})v^2\,\mathrm d\mu_S$.

Every nonnegative compactly supported smooth function $f$ on the closed regular side, with support avoiding the singular set, satisfies $$\label{cut:deletion}
       \int_S f\,\mathrm d\mu_S
       \le\int_\Omega\bigl(|\mathop{\mathrm{grad}}f|+p_sf\bigr)\,\mathrm d\mu.$$ For every smooth real test $v$ of the same type, $$\label{cut:side-form}
 3.05\int_\Omega|\mathop{\mathrm{grad}}v|^2\,\mathrm d\mu
       +2\int_S H_{\rm out}v^2\,\mathrm d\mu_S
       \ge-1.02\int_\Omega\Pi_{j_0}v^2\,\mathrm d\mu.$$ Both statements extend to compactly supported Lipschitz tests by approximation.

Let $F$ be a compact subset of $\Sigma\cap\{h_j>t_j\}$. For every sufficiently small $\varepsilon>0$ there is an extended-real profile $u_\varepsilon$, equal to $+\infty$ for $\delta\le\varepsilon$ and $-\infty$ for $\delta\ge R_\varepsilon$, where $$\delta(x)=\mathop{\mathrm{dist}}(x,F),\qquad R_\varepsilon=e^{5\pi}\varepsilon,$$ whose finite truncations are locally Lipschitz and which satisfies $$\label{local:shell-gradient}
 2|\nabla u_\varepsilon|
       \le .58u_\varepsilon^2+2\delta^{-2}
       \quad (\varepsilon<\delta<R_\varepsilon).$$ There is a smooth nonnegative ambient function $D_\varepsilon$ with $$\label{local:shell-potential}
 \begin{aligned}
 D_\varepsilon&\ge2\delta^{-2}
       &&\text{on }\{\varepsilon\le\delta\le R_\varepsilon\},\\
 D_\varepsilon&\le2.12\delta^{-2}
       &&\text{everywhere off }F,\\
 \mathop{\mathrm{supp}}D_\varepsilon&\subset
       \{\varepsilon/2<\delta<2R_\varepsilon\}
       \Subset\{h_j>t_j\}.
 \end{aligned}$$ Replacing $\mu_j$ by $\max(\mu_j,u_\varepsilon)$, adding $D_\varepsilon$ to $\Pi_j$, and adding $\{\delta<\varepsilon/2\}$ to $U_j^+$ preserves the profile inequality with coefficient $a_r$. There is an identical negative construction in $\{h_j<t_j\}$, using $\min(\mu_j,-u_\varepsilon)$ and enlarging $U_j^-$. All supports and newly forced regions are compactly contained in the stated strict anchor region.

For each $m\ge8$ there are numbers $\eta_0>0$ and $c_0>0$ with the following property. Suppose $F$ satisfies <a href="#local:flatness" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="local:flatness">[local:flatness]</a> with $\eta\le\eta_0$ in a sufficiently accurate buffered chart. There are $d_F>0$ and $C_F<\infty$ such that, on the wall and on either joined side, $$\label{local:rough-estimate}
 c_0\int_{\delta<d_F}\delta^{-2}v^2
             \le\mathcal N(v)+C_F\|v\|_2^2.$$ The constants $\eta_0,c_0$ depend only on $m$ and a fixed permitted chart distortion. The constants $d_F,C_F$ may depend on the compact piece, its scale threshold, and the local smooth metric, weight, and pressure. No principal-curvature bound for the wall is assumed.

There is a sufficiently small flatness number $\eta>0$, depending only on $m$ and the fixed numerical coefficients, with the following property. Let $F$ be any piece from <a href="#local:flat-pieces" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="local:flat-pieces">49</a> for this flatness number, in a sufficiently accurate chart. For the potential of <a href="#local:shell" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="local:shell">50</a>, there are $\varepsilon_F>0$ and $C_F<\infty$ such that, for every $0<\varepsilon<\varepsilon_F$, $$\label{local:sharp-estimate}
 1.16\int D_\varepsilon v^2
           \le .78\mathcal N(v)+C_F\|v\|_2^2.$$ This holds on the true wall and either joined side, and hence on translated compact tests in a pure wall cylinder. The constants $\varepsilon_F,C_F$ may depend on the local smooth data and $F$, but are independent of $\varepsilon$. No vanishing trace condition is imposed at a joined seam.

Fix a packet and its true pieces. Let $V\ge0$ be a fixed bounded potential, pulled back to cylinders, satisfying $$\label{shield:old-bound}
 \int_Z Vv^2\le\theta\mathfrak h_Z(v)$$ on its wall and both joined sides. Let $F\subset\Sigma$ be a compact piece and let $A_\varepsilon=1.16D_\varepsilon$ be one of the nonnegative shell potentials of [local:shell,local:sharp] [local:shell](#local:shell), [local:sharp](#local:sharp). In particular its base support lies in a fixed compact set and shrinks to $F$, and $$\label{shield:local-input}
 \int_Z A_\varepsilon v^2\le .78\mathcal N_Z(v)+C_F\norm v_2^2$$ for all sufficiently small $\varepsilon$, on all three pieces. For every $\eta>0$, a sufficiently small $\varepsilon>0$ gives simultaneously $$\label{shield:maximum-bound}
 \int_Z(V+A_\varepsilon)v^2
 \le\bigl(\max\{\theta,.78\}+\eta\bigr)\mathfrak h_Z(v).$$ It suffices that $V$ be bounded on the compact base windows used below. In particular the assertion applies to a finite sum of compact additions on the initial radial parent.

Let $B$ be a packet, let $D\ge0$ be a fixed smooth compactly supported potential addition on $B$, and let $V$ denote the old cumulative potential on every packet. Suppose these old potentials are exactly compatible and obey the common form bound $\theta\mathfrak h$. Suppose also that $$\int(V_B+1.16D)v^2\le\beta\mathfrak h_B(v),\qquad \beta\ge\theta,$$ on the wall and joined sides over $B$. In each of the finitely many coface occurrences $B\times(T,\infty)^d\subset E$, introduce a smooth potential $D_E$ with $$\label{shield:extension-support}
 0\le D_E\le D\circ\pi_B,\qquad
 \mathop{\mathrm{supp}}D_E\subset K\times\prod_{i=1}^d[R_i,\infty),
 \qquad K\Subset B.$$ Use consistent functions on the normal coordinates identified by commuting face chains, so that these extensions are compatible. For every $\eta>0$ all starts can be chosen sufficiently large that $$\label{shield:extended-bound}
 \int(V_E+1.16D_E)v^2\le(\beta+\eta)\mathfrak h_E(v)$$ on every affected raw piece. The conclusion concerns the same fixed true cuts; it uses their product convergence from <a href="#cut:end-convergence" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="cut:end-convergence">43</a>.

At a fixed stage $r$, let $j_0$ be the current label and keep its true minimizers fixed. There are updates of every remaining profile and core, and compatible smooth additions $D_j\ge0$, with the following properties on every parent packet $E$ of dimension $m$:*


1.  *The updated profiles have locally Lipschitz finite truncations and satisfy, almost everywhere on their finite bands, $$\label{shield:profile-output}
     2\abs{\nabla\mu'_j}\le a_r(\mu'_j)^2+\Pi_j+D_j.$$ All these data are exact compatible products. Each core only enlarges, and its closure remains in the interior of its designated updated pole set. The original forced sets and the anchor sign restrictions are preserved.*

2.  *With $G'_j=E\setminus(U_j^{\prime+}\cup U_j^{\prime-})$, the set $$\label{shield:guard-output}
     H_E^*=\left\{x:\#\{j\ne j_0:x\in G'_j\}\ge m-2\right\}$$ is closed and misses $\Sigma_E$. In an exact collar over a face $B$, its projection is contained in $H_B^*$. This holds for every further face and every simultaneous product limit.*


3.  *For one common $\theta_*<.9$, all walls and joined sides satisfy $$\label{shield:form-output}
     \int 1.16\sum_{j\ne j_0}D_jv^2
     \le\theta_*\bigl(\mathcal N(v)+e_0\norm v_2^2\bigr)
     \le .9\bigl(\mathcal N(v)+e_0\norm v_2^2\bigr).$$ The additions are bounded with their derivatives on each post-radial packet. There are only finitely many local additions on each such packet and only finitely many extensions into it.*

*For the initial radial parent the same conclusions hold with locally finite additions over its compact transition shells; boundedness is asserted on the corresponding compact blocks and <a href="#shield:form-output" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="shield:form-output">[shield:form-output]</a> holds on every compact test. No convergence assertion at an end of the original manifold is needed.
